# synthetic-userinput-clarify.jsonl — PART wire capture, PART hand-written.
#
# The CLARIFY path — the person answers a `request_user_input` prompt with
# "let me explain instead" rather than picking an option — was never captured
# live. Only the ANSWER path was (`transcript-userinput-answer.jsonl`, one real
# `meta` turn), and a second live turn to get a clarification would have spent
# another one for a settlement whose only difference from the answered one is
# three fields.
#
# So: every line down to and including `userInput/requested` is verbatim from
# that real capture — the request the provider actually minted. From the
# `userInput/clarify` command on, the lines are hand-written to the shapes in
# `fixtures/msp/msp-ts/msp.d.ts`: `outcome: "clarified"`, `answers: []`, and a
# `clarification` object with `content` and `format`. The fold reads a
# settlement with a clarification and no chosen option as
# `QuestionOutcome::Clarified`, which is what the answered row then says.
#
# Named `synthetic-` so nobody mistakes the second half for the wire.
